  "goodToKnow": "Die Kreuzigung is crucifixion, especially die Kreuzigung Jesu, remembered on Karfreitag (Good Friday), a public holiday when dancing is restricted in many states (Tanzverbot). The village of Oberammergau has performed its Passionsspiele, including the crucifixion, about every ten years since 1634, after a vow during the plague. Grünewald's Isenheim Altarpiece shows a famous Kreuzigung. Plural: die Kreuzigungen."
